From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:40:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: apple: describe the deep-sleep fields of the J604
 host-keeping changes

The T8132 host-keeping changes added three struct members without a
kernel-doc line, so W=1 warns about them:

  dwc3-apple.c: struct member 'sleep_reset_resume' not described in 'dwc3_apple'
  dwc3-apple.c: struct member 'sleep_lost' not described in 'dwc3_apple'
  atc.c: struct member 'sleep_lose' not described in 'apple_atcphy'

Describe them in the structs' kernel-doc blocks, in the words of the
comments already next to them. Comments only; no object changes.

The other 17 undescribed members in these two structs come from the
ports-sleep changes (hub_check, hub_port, pm_nb, sleep_* in dwc3_apple;
hibernated, sleep_in_place, sleep_no_keep, sleep_ret, sleep_ss_down and
the t8132_* fields in apple_atcphy) and are left to that series.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c       | 2 ++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index acc09b540e..16d9c9b023 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -777,6 +777,8 @@ enum atcphy_t8132_cio_tunable {
  *              it when the PHY is brought back up after a power-off
  * @host_active: dwc3 has selected host mode on the USB3 PHY; a fixed-hub port
  *               then routes the PIPE itself on later Type-C mode changes
+ * @sleep_lose: The host loses its power in this system sleep and comes back in place,
+ *              see apple_atcphy_sleep_lose_prepare()
  * @usb3_port_off: The SuperSpeed root port of a fixed-hub controller was powered
  *                 off for a PIPE or lane change and is not powered on again yet
  * @usb3_port_work: Retries the power-on of @usb3_port_off after a USB failure
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index ba99020a1c..20b3799610 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -139,6 +139,9 @@
  * @rpm_held: The glue holds a runtime PM reference for the running core
  * @pre_core_rpm: Runtime PM is the glue's own until the first core bring-up
  * @dt_dis_u3_susphy: The device tree keeps USB3 PHY suspend off itself
+ * @sleep_reset_resume: A T8132 host is kept registered through a deep sleep that may cut
+ *                      its power, see dwc3_apple_t8132_reset_resume()
+ * @sleep_lost: The resume of such a host found its power gone
  */
 struct dwc3_apple {
 	struct dwc3 dwc;
